Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.32,0:00:03.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Those gaps are where this film lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.10,0:00:06.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The study behind this\Nfilm asks three things.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.38,0:00:11.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One: can a {\c&HF09CB4&}machine{\c&HF7F4F2&} learn\Nthe whole family of fields,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.35,0:00:14.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}even at knob settings between the dots?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.63,0:00:17.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Two: can it respect\Neach law where it holds,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.00,0:00:22.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}exactly in every field,\Nor {\c&H00A1ED&}on average{\c&HF7F4F2&} over many fields?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.51,0:00:26.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Three: can it tell us\N{\c&H00A1ED&}how often{\c&HF7F4F2&} the field flips?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.19,0:00:30.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}To find out, the study's\Nplan climbs a staircase,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.60,0:00:34.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}from three numbers to the\Nshapes of real experiments.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.49,0:00:38.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One honest note: this\Nindependent study is prospective,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.93,0:00:42.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}built on small experiments\Non an ordinary computer,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.12,0:00:46.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}and not endorsed by MilaDy,\Nits partners or the supervisors.
